</tr>
<tr>
    <td  bgcolor="#c0c0c0" valign="TOP"><table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" border="0">
<tr>
    <td  bgcolor="#c0c0c0" width="100%" valign="top"><tt><font color="#000000">
Author:&nbsp;<a href="/showmember.php?name=Eldaronmyth">Eldaronmyth</a>&nbsp;(63.180.42.---)<br>
Date:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;06-30-01 15:40<br>
<br><HTML>Wandering thru West Commons (as I am wont to do after consuming a stack of Double <br>
Strength Dwarven Ale) I stumbled upon a camp of Dark Elves that I didn't recall <br>
being there before(they might have been there before... like I said, lotsa <br>
alcohol). They all conned indifferent to my Dwarven Paladin. When hailed, I got <br>
a response along the lines of "Can't talk to you, now begone, or feel the combined<br>
 might of Fuzzy Bunny Slippers! (I THINK that's what they said, my Tier'Dal is <br>
a little fuzzy, as was my vision)<br>
I learned there were three such camps. Funny thing was, I hit 'U', and got the <br>
"You can't reach that". In the camp by the shadow men, you click on a pot, it <br>
turns, and you hear a door open. Other 2 camps it was the tent poles... none of <br>
the items replied to questioning. (REMEMBER! Drunk Dwarf!)<br>
There was a name mentioned tho (might have been an NPC, or the tent talking to <br>
me); Natoxys. Now I seem to remember something in lore about him and Lanys <br>
(Inny's 50 foot tall daughter from an event about 6 months back), which was <br>
linked to Amiaz in Befallen. So I went to Befallen.<br>
<br>
So I walk into Befallen, trusty Ghoulbane in hand (Hell, coulda been a corndog <br>
at this point, alcohol was in full effect)and immediately get beset upon by Dark <br>
Elves screaming something about 'The Dark Lady'. Well, they were spoiling my buzz, <br>
so I popped open a Keg of Brell's Finest Whoopass on em. When the dust cleared <br>
(Nothing clears dust like a fine Dwarven brew induced, toe curling, belch) I <br>
noticed a few things different. One, there were a LOT more Dark Elves than I <br>
remembered. Two, there was a lack of wimpy skeletons(Fun to tease "NYAH NYAH, <br>
you call that a 'BOO'???". Three, there were a LOT more corpses of adventurers <br>
cluttering the entrance area. Four, in my drunken stupor, I seem to have mislaid <br>
my pants.<br>
<br>
After finding my pants (which were, oddly enough, on my head) and putting on my <br>
helm (don't ask where IT was...)I decided to venture forth into the dungeon. Many <br>
were the shouts of "WTF? Where'd the SK's go?!" and "AIEEEE!!! Train to zone!!!"<br>
As I was trying to fit the key to the lock of the first door, I received a tap on <br>
the shoulder(for 41 damage, a mild surprise at this point in the dungeon...) from <br>
a helpful fellow by the name of 'A Dark Follower'. He seemed to think that I'd get <br>
thru the door a lot easier in small pieces... I thought different.<br>
<br>
After cleaning my blade, I managed to fit the damn key in the keyhole (Which DOES <br>
get smaller in direct proportion to how many beer you have)and opened the door to <br>
a host of friendly undead. George (My Ghoulbane. He picked the name, not me) zinged<br>
 with glee at the mass of undead. After clearing the way to the spike room and the <br>
intersection beyond, I was met with yet another surprise.<br>
<br>
I ran into finely dressed Ogres and half elves mingling. I said to myself "Self, <br>
this is odd." Self agreed. I offered these gents some fine ale, but they must have <br>
left their manners at the Union Hall, and proceeded to try to take ALL my beer, for <br>
their 'Dark Lady'. Needless to say, I was not impressed, and proceeded to thwack <br>
yon hoodlums betwixt head and toe. I managed to venture throughout the entire second <br>
floor, but for the life of me couldn't find the third key.(I later found out that <br>
you apparantely no longer need a key for the bottom door... might be right, might <br>
be wrong). At this point in time, the one man "Drinkfest become raid" had to be <br>
delayed due to lack of beer...and the fact that there were so many people in the <br>
zone I couldn't do anything without tripping over someone. I plan to return with <br>
fresh kegs tomorrow eve (perhaps) and see what lies on the third floor. <br>
Till then, may Brell keep your glass at least half full, never empty.<br>
<br>
*Wanders off in search of cheese and asbestos underwear*<br>
<br>
<br>
Bakamur Longlere<br>
Paladin of the Keg</HTML></font></tt><p>
